  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MULTI-INSTITUTIONAL INTEGRATED INITIATIVE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will: 1) Enhance (635 has)/(1568.45 acres) at Cuitzeo Lake through the construction of a new wastewater treatment plant and the rehabilitation of the last section of the wastewater treatment plant for town of Cuitzeo; construction of a sanitary drainage and sewer system in the city of Morelia; development of integrated sanitation projects for 3 municipalities within the watershed; installation of 100 dry toilets; and construction of structures for soil conservation to reduce the contribution of sediments to the lake. 2) Install signs in the UMA previously established by the grantee and fence 2.5 Km of a previously restored area. 3) Monitor habitat quality; monitor waterfowl and shorebirds using the lake; monitor aquatic beds in the lake; evaluate the efficiency of waste removal in 4 wastewater treatment plants; and analyze water quality in the urban water supply of Huandacareo and Copandaro .4) Train 200 teachers and reach 2,000 children through Teaching the Teachers environmental education training workshops; train 125 farmers in alternative, environmentally friendly techniques; and offer training courses to municipal water operating agencies</narrative>
  </description>
